  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Web App Scope**\n\nOkay, I\'m starting to grasp the user\'s vision. I\'m focusing on the \"Industrial Precision\" design system and the four provided screenshots as blueprints for a web application. I\'m breaking down the project into manageable components: Data Quality, Equipment Explorer, AI Assistant, and Fleet Management. My initial goal is a foundational understanding of the project\'s scope.\n\n\n**Pinpointing Key Technical Details**\n\nI\'ve established the technical foundation. I\'m focusing on incorporating React, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS. The file tree will follow a standard Vite setup, with React and TypeScript. HMR is disabled. I\'m taking notes on required dependencies. I\'m focusing on the \"Industrial Precision\" design system, ensuring a dark mode first approach. I have all the design system details, including colors and fonts.\n\n\n**Clarifying Project Structure**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the application\'s core architecture. Recognizing those provided HTML snippets as representations of the app\'s views, I\'m focusing on a single-page application structure. The layout will involve a Sidebar and Main Content area. Routing will be state-based for this demo, utilizing an `activeTab` variable. Key components I\'m considering are a `Layout` component encompassing the `Sidebar` and `TopBar`, plus individual pages for the `FleetOverview` and `EquipmentExplorer`.\n\n\n**Outlining Component Breakdown**\n\nI\'m now identifying core components for implementation. Key views will include `AIAssistant`, `DataQuality`, and an `EquipmentDetail` view triggered by equipment row clicks. I\'m also planning for essential shared components like `Card`, `Badge`, and `ProgressBar`, plus icons from `lucide-react`.\n\nI\'m setting up Tailwind and Fonts next, incorporating IBM Plex Sans and Mono from Google Fonts, and configuring Tailwind with the design system\'s colors. After that, I\'ll build core layout components and then the pages for the main views.\n\n\n**Adding Agent Activity View**\n\nI\'m now integrating an Agent Activity panel alongside the existing components. Specifically, I\'m focusing on implementing the `DataQuality.tsx` view with KPIs, a Heatmap placeholder, sync logs, and rejected records. I\'m also ensuring an `EquipmentDetail.tsx` view for individual pump data. I\'m moving toward state-based navigation and implementing a detailed plan for that.\n\n\n**Planning File Management**\n\nNow, I\'m defining the necessary file operations. I\'ll start by adding fonts to `index.html`. Then, I will focus on Tailwind theme overrides in `src/index.css`. Next, I will create `src/types.ts` for shared interfaces. I will also create essential components and pages. Finally, I will wire everything up in `src/App.tsx`, followed by linting and compilation.\n\n\n**Building the Components**\n\nI\'m now getting started with the development, with `vite` and `tailwind` set up. I\'m focusing on the overall application layout, starting with `flex-row` for layout, and the fixed-width `Sidebar` and flexible `Main Content` area. My next step will be to define navigation state using `activeView` to manage component rendering. I\'m now looking at building the components, starting with folder structure.\n\n\n**Defining the Component Structure**\n\nI\'m now generating the necessary file structure for the app\'s building blocks. I\'m focusing on defining the `types.ts` file, and creating Sidebar, TopBar, and main pages for FleetOverview, EquipmentExplorer, AIAssistant, DataQuality, and EquipmentDetail. Also, I\'ll update the `index.html` to include the IBM Plex fonts, and create `src/index.css` to manage theme customization using Tailwind\'s `@theme` directive. Finally, I will edit `src/App.tsx`. I\'m also refining the design for a clean look.\n\n\n**Constructing UI Element Outlines**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the individual components and pages within the application. I\'m building out the sidebar with active state styling for navigation. I\'m focusing on the individual views. I\'m planning out the `FleetOverview`, including KPIs, a donut chart (I\'ll implement this with SVG), and an action-required table. Then, I\'ll move on to `EquipmentExplorer`, `AIAssistant`, `DataQuality`, and `EquipmentDetail`, defining their core structures. I will begin by working on index.html, index.css, and types.ts.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Page Implementation**\n\nI\'m now changing my focus to page implementation. I\'ve realized the prompt prioritizes visual fidelity, so I\'ll build out `FleetOverview` and `EquipmentExplorer` first. I\'m batching file creations to improve workflow: `index.html`, `index.css`, and `types.ts` form the first batch, followed by the Layout components, then the prioritized pages. I\'m focusing on simplicity, using the provided Tailwind colors from the HTML head. I\'ll translate the user\'s config to CSS `@theme` vars.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 27
      nanos: 410934848
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
